@startuml
title Layers of control around an AI agent

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "9. Cloud guardrails\nrights, deletion protection, budget (document 06-06)" as L9 #F4F7F9 {
  rectangle "8. Repository and pipeline\nprotected main branch, gates, review by a person" as L8 #E3F2FD {
    rectangle "7. Identity\nno token or credential that can change the cloud" as L7 #E3F2FD {
      rectangle "6. Hooks\na program decides before a tool runs" as L6 #C8E6C9 {
        rectangle "5. Permission rules\nallowed, asked, never" as L5 #C8E6C9 {
          rectangle "4. Sandbox\nfiles and network of ordinary commands" as L4 #C8E6C9 {
            rectangle "3. Session account\nnothing of the developer is on it" as L3 #FFE0B2 {
              rectangle "2. Managed settings\nthe company's policy, not overridable" as L2 #FFF8E1 {
                rectangle "1. Data path and terms\nwhat leaves the workstation" as L1 #FFF8E1 {
                  component "Agent\n(model + tools)" as A #FFFFFF
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

note bottom of L9
  Layers 1 to 6 are on the workstation: the harness itself.
  Layers 7 to 9 are outside it and do not depend on it.
  Layer 3 is what makes the others safe to fail: an agent
  that escapes them finds nothing but the repository.
end note
@enduml
